# Results stay local: this repo is code plus the Run 1 handoff docs, nothing
# else. Both of these were published by a `git add docs/` -- a DIRECTORY, not a
# file -- that swept up far more than the one doc it was aimed at. It happened
# twice, the second time one commit after this comment was first written, which
# is why OVERNIGHT.md is untracked now rather than merely kept-in-sync: a
# tracked file whose working copy permanently differs from HEAD cannot be
# protected by .gitignore, and every `add -A` / `add <dir>` / `commit -a` puts
# it back. Stage explicit file paths.
docs/measurements/overnight/
docs/OVERNIGHT.md

# upstream checkout (setup_env.sh clones it here); never ours to commit
third_party/
# local CPU-only venv for running the no-GPU gates without renting a box
.venv-cpu/

# upstream checkout (setup_env.sh clones it here); never ours to commit
third_party/
